arbeitnow:senior-scrum-master-core-video:
&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Hudl, we build great teams. We hire the best of the best to ensure you’re working with people you can constantly learn from. You’re trusted to get your work done your way while testing the limits of what’s possible and what’s next. We work hard to provide a culture where everyone feels supported, and our employees feel it—their votes helped us become one of &lt;a href="https://www.hudl.com/blog/newsweek-top-100-global-most-loved-workplaces-2023"&gt;Newsweek's Top 100 Global Most Loved Workplaces&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We think of ourselves as the team behind the team, supporting the lifelong impact sports can have: the lessons in teamwork and dedication; the influence of inspiring coaches; and the opportunities to reach new heights. That’s why we help teams from all over the world see their game differently. Our products make it easier for coaches and athletes at any level to capture video, analyze data, share highlights and more.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Ready to join us?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div style="padding: 56.25% 0 0 0; position: relative;"&gt;&lt;iframe style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: 0;" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/1095624224?h=9e8cdc9dbe&amp;amp;badge=0&amp;amp;autopause=0&amp;amp;player_id=0&amp;amp;app_id=58479" width="" height=""&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Your Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We're looking for a Senior Scrum Master to join our team in London. Our products help the world's top teams and athletes perform at their best. We need an experienced Agile leader to help the squads building them do the same.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior ScrumMaster, you'll:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coach the system, not just the team.&lt;/strong&gt; You'll guide squads toward high autonomy while focusing on broader organizational design issues, such as resolving friction across business units, managing dependencies, and establishing scaling patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architect outcomes, not processes.&lt;/strong&gt; You'll move fluidly across frameworks, adapting events to what the team needs to deliver value. You will act as an outcome architect, designing information flow and decision rhythms rather than functioning as a framework fundamentalist.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Anticipate, not react.&lt;/strong&gt; You'll utilize predictive delivery intelligence and cross-team dependency mapping to resolve impediments before they surface, keeping coordination moving in the right direction even as the pace of delivery accelerates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foster psychological safety.&lt;/strong&gt; You'll build environments where candor is safe, failure is treated as a data point, and conflict is constructive. You'll ensure teams feel secure enough to take on hard problems and navigate the shifting dynamics brought on by AI-assisted development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Align and design for visibility.&lt;/strong&gt; You'll map value streams to see where decisions stall and design cross-BU communication layers. You will maintain the signal through the noise, ensuring stakeholders know what's changed and what decisions are needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Time spent collaborating with your teammates in-office will be a regular part of how you work. We're currently considering applicants within commuting distance of our London office. You'll be expected to work more days in-office than remote, but will have the freedom to coordinate your specific in-office schedule with your team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Must-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An experienced Agile practitioner. &lt;/strong&gt;You have three or more years as a Scrum Master and have guided squads to improved, sustainable results and can scale your coaching capacity to influence broader organizational maturity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A systems thinker.&lt;/strong&gt; You see beyond the squad level, actively identifying and breaking down siloed organizational designs to reduce friction and eliminate duplicated efforts across Business Units.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-driven and predictive. &lt;/strong&gt;You know how to use both qualitative and quantitative signals to establish predictive metrics that forecast delivery risk and guide investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A clear communicator.&lt;/strong&gt; You design lightweight operating guardrails and information flows that keep dependencies transparent and align stakeholders at every level without creating overhead that slows teams down.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A champion of responsible speed.&lt;/strong&gt; You optimize for quality, anticipated dependencies, commitments kept, and team sustainability, ensuring that the speed of code generation never outpaces our coordination speed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice-to-Haves&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI fluency.&lt;/strong&gt; You have an interest in or experience with AI-assisted development tools and AI-powered agile tools, such as automated bottleneck detection or real-time sentiment and health monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A diverse Agile toolbelt. &lt;/strong&gt;You're familiar with multiple frameworks (Kanban, Lean, SAFe, etc) and know when and how to blend them for better outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global team experience. &lt;/strong&gt;Our product teams span the U.S. and Europe, and you're comfortable collaborating across time zones and cultures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion work-life harmony&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;. We’ll give you the flexibility you need in your work life (e.g., flexible vacation time, company-wide holidays and timeout (meeting-free) days, remote work options and more) so you can enjoy your personal life too.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Guarantee autonomy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;. We have an open, honest culture and we trust our people from day one. Your team will support you, but you’ll own your work and have the agency to try new ideas.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Encourage career growth&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;. We’re lifelong learners who encourage professional development. We’ll give you tons of resources and opportunities to keep growing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Provide an environment to help you succeed&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;. We've invested in our offices, designing incredible spaces with our employees in mind. But whether you’re at the office or working remotely, we’ll provide you the tech stack and hardware to do your best work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support your wellbeing. &lt;/strong&gt;Depending on location, we offer medical and retirement benefits for employees—but no matter where you’re located, we have resources like our Employee Assistance Program and employee resource groups to support your mental health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;div class="content-pay-transparency"&gt;&lt;div class="pay-input"&gt;&lt;div class="description"&gt;&lt;p&gt;The base salary range for this role is displayed below—&lt;strong&gt;starting salaries will typically fall near the middle of this range.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make compensation decisions based on an individual's experience, skills and education in line with our internal pay equity practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will also be eligible for a long-term incentive (LTI) award. Any bonuses awarded are based on individual and company performance paid at Hudl's discretion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="title"&gt;Base Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="pay-range"&gt;&lt;span&gt;£48,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="divider"&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;£80,000 GBP&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="content-conclusion"&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inclusion at Hudl&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hudl is an equal opportunity employer. Through our actions, behaviors and attitude, we’ll create an environment where everyone, no matter their differences, feels like they belong.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We offer resources to ensure our employees feel safe bringing their authentic selves to work, &lt;a href="https://www.hudl.com/about-inclusion" target="_blank"&gt;including employee resource groups and communities&lt;/a&gt;. But we recognize there’s ongoing work to be done, which is why we track our efforts and commitments in &lt;a href="https://www.hudl.com/about-inclusion" target="_blank"&gt;annual inclusion reports&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;We also know imposter syndrome is real and the &lt;a href="https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2014/05/the-confidence-gap/359815/" target="_blank"&gt;confidence gap&lt;/a&gt; can get in the way of meeting spectacular candidates. Please don’t hesitate to apply—we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.hudl.com/jobs/hudl-applicant-and-candidate-privacy-policy"&gt;&lt;span style="font-weight: 400;"&gt;Hudl Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</p>

arbeitnow:software-engineer-intern-londo:
&lt;div class="content-intro"&gt;&lt;p&gt;Figma is growing our team of passionate creatives and builders on a mission to make design accessible to all. Figma’s platform helps teams bring ideas to life—whether you're brainstorming, creating a prototype, translating designs into code, or iterating with AI. From idea to product, Figma empowers teams to streamline workflows, move faster, and work together in real time from anywhere in the world. If you're excited to shape the future of design and collaboration, join us!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for software engineering interns who are excited to make an impact across different layers of our product and infrastructure. At Figma, we pair interns with teams that align with their skills and interests. This year, we're inviting you to share your interests from the start, so we can create the strongest possible match.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our interns are embedded into small, collaborative engineering teams across the company. You’ll work closely with your mentor and teammates to ship meaningful features, tools, or systems. Whether you're working on internal infrastructure or user-facing features, you’ll get to learn, contribute, and grow in a supportive environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This internship will be based out of our London Hub with a 5/3, 5/17, 6/1 or 6/14 start date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Interests at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When you apply, you'll tell us which areas you're most interested in to help us understand which kinds of engineering work you're most excited about:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product: Build full stack user facing features, including new collaboration tools, new product workflows, growth oriented experiments, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform/Infrastructure: Build platform level tools, including distributed systems, developer tooling, performance/scalability work, and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security Engineering: Build security-focused systems, product security tooling, detection, secure infrastructure, or privacy/security features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open: I’m flexible and still exploring different types of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you'll do at Figma:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join a small engineering team as a full member of the team, with your own project and mentor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to projects that directly align with team goals and impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with engineers, PMs, designers, and QA to break down features and plan timelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, document, and maintain tests, features, or infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Share feedback and participate in peer code review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship your project(s) by the end of your internship!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some past intern projects:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://x.com/peterdpong/status/1554514887052693504?s=21&amp;amp;t=WNnRrJF5DRxo0EcNopDj1Q"&gt;Diagramming improvements in FigJam&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.figma.com/blog/introducing-smart-selection/"&gt;Smart selection&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="https://help.figma.com/hc/en-us/articles/360039956774-Upload-custom-fonts-to-an-organization"&gt;Shared fonts&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’d love to hear from you if you have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing clean code in at least one general-purpose language (e.g. C++, JavaScript, Python, Java, etc.), with a solid grasp of core CS concepts like data structures and algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience solving technical problems through school, work, or personal projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted development tools (e.g., GitHub Copilot, ChatGPT, Claude) to write, debug, and optimize code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated curiosity about how systems are designed and operate, from infrastructure to UI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator who asks great questions, collaborates well with others, and is excited to learn, get feedback, and grow as an engineer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Figma, one of our values is Grow as you go. We believe in hiring smart, curious people who are excited to learn and develop their skills. If you’re excited about this role but your past experience doesn’t align perfectly with the points outlined in the job description, we encourage you to apply anyways. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="content-conclusion"&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Figma we celebrate and support our differences. We know employing a team rich in diverse thoughts, experiences, and opinions allows our employees, our product and our community to flourish. Figma is an &lt;a href="https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2022-10/EEOC_KnowYourRights_screen_reader_10_20.pdf"&gt;equal opportunity workplace&lt;/a&gt; - we are dedicated to equal employment opportunities regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity/expression, veteran status&lt;strong&gt;, &lt;/strong&gt;or any other characteristic protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will work to ensure individuals with disabilities are provided reasonable accommodation to apply for a role, participate in the interview process, perform essential job functions, and receive other benefits and privileges of employment. If you require accommodation, please reach out to &lt;a ---------- These modifications enable an individual with a disability to have an equal opportunity not only to get a job, but successfully perform their job tasks to the same extent as people without disabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Examples of accommodations include but are not limited to:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Holding interviews in an accessible location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enabling closed captioning on video conferencing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring all written communication be compatible with screen readers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Changing the mode or format of interviews&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To ensure the integrity of our hiring process and facilitate a more personal connection, we require all candidates keep their cameras on during video interviews. Additionally, if hired you will be required to attend in person onboarding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By applying for this job, the candidate acknowledges and agrees that any personal data contained in their application or supporting materials will be processed in accordance with &lt;a class="c-link c-link--underline" href="https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/" target="_blank" data-stringify-link="https://www.figma.com/legal/candidate-privacy-notice/" data-sk="tooltip_parent"&gt;Figma's Candidate Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</p>

arbeitnow:principal-backbone-edge-archit:
&lt;h2&gt;About Nscale&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nscale is the GPU cloud engineered for AI. We provide cost-effective, high-performance infrastructure for AI start-ups and large enterprise customers. Nscale enables AI-focused companies to achieve superior results by reducing the complexity of AI development. Our GPU cloud bolsters technical capabilities and directly supports strategic business outcomes, including cost management, rapid innovation, and environmental responsibility.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nscale, our AI Infrastructure team plays a critical role in building the global network infrastructure that powers our GPU cloud platform, enabling reliable, high-performance connectivity across our data centres, customers, cloud partners, and global backbone.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We thrive on a culture of relentless innovation, ownership, and accountability, where every team member takes pride in their work and drives it with excellence and urgency. As an Nscaler, you'll build trust through openness and transparency, where everyone is inspired to do their best work. If you join our team, you'll be contributing to building the technology that powers the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are hiring a Principal Network Backbone &amp;amp; Edge Architect to serve as the senior technical design authority for Nscale's global network infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will design, validate, and own the technical standards governing our transport networks — from GPU data centre edge through WAN and backbone transport to cloud exchange connectivity and Internet peering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly influential individual contributor role. While you won't have direct reports, your architectural decisions will define what gets built, how it gets built, and how Nscale's global network evolves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You'll work across our global network organisation and engage directly with carriers, technology vendors, hyperscalers, and enterprise customers. We're looking for someone equally comfortable developing detailed architecture and design standards, evaluating emerging network technologies, and being hands-on in a data centre validating a new backbone node.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you'll be doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Architecture &amp;amp; Standards&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own and maintain Nscale's global network architecture standards across DC edge, WAN edge, backbone transport, cloud exchange, OOB/management, and automation architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead the design of new network infrastructure deployments across regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Produce detailed network designs, topology documentation, IP addressing schemes, and routing policy frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define technology selection criteria and lead vendor and technology evaluations for major network infrastructure decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Conduct architecture reviews for significant network changes, ensuring alignment with global standards before implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute network architecture requirements to data centre design reviews from the earliest stages of new facility planning.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technology Strategy &amp;amp; Roadmap&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own Nscale's network technology roadmap.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify and evaluate emerging capabilities including 800G/1.6T coherent optics, AI-driven network operations, and next-generation cloud exchange integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Produce and maintain technology horizon documentation to inform investment planning and strategic supplier discussions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Evaluate and recommend technologies, vendors, and platforms aligned with Nscale's commercial objectives, operating model, and growth plans.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Technical Governance&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the final technical authority for major network design decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Review and approve significant network designs before implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify technical risks within proposed architectures and drive resolution before they reach production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maintain and evolve Nscale's network design standards library, ensuring documentation remains current and actionable across regions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Supplier &amp;amp; Customer Engagement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engage directly with strategic technology and connectivity partners on architecture roadmaps, capabilities, and technical partnerships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support enterprise customer and hyperscaler engagements, including architecture walkthroughs, connectivity design reviews, and technical due diligence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work with carrier and colocation partners on complex challenges including multi-site diversity, capacity planning, and technology evolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with Product and Sales teams to translate network architecture capabilities into customer-facing value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12+ years of network engineering experience, including at least 4 years in a senior architecture or Principal Engineering role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep expertise in large-scale IP/MPLS network design, SRv6, IPv6, BGP, traffic engineering, and multi-AS routing architectures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proven experience designing carrier-grade backbone and WAN infrastructure for hyperscale or large-scale data centre environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on expertise with Nokia SR routing platforms and coherent optical transport architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong working knowledge of data centre fabric architecture, cloud exchange platforms, and customer connectivity design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with network automation architecture, including OpenConfig, NETCONF, YANG, and API-driven infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong ability to produce high-quality architecture designs, technical documentation, and standards frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Track record of strategic vendor and technology evaluation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience engaging enterprise customers and hyperscalers in technical architecture discussions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Knowledge of carrier ecosystems across EMEA, APAC, and the Americas is strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we can offer you&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nscale, you'll find a collaborative, supportive, and innovative environment where your contributions spark real impact. We're building something extraordinary, and we want you at the core.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Highly competitive package (base + equity) with reviews every 12 months. 🚀&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join one of the fastest-growing AI infrastructure companies — your opportunity to define the global network architecture powering the next generation of AI. ✨&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Expect a dynamic progression plan tailored to your ambitions. Shape technical strategy, evaluate emerging technologies, and influence how Nscale's global network evolves as we scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Human-First Flexibility: We treat you as humans first. 🫶🏽 Our flexible workplace trusts Nscalers to deliver, giving you the autonomy to shape your day around life's moments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equal Opportunities Statement&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We strongly encourage applications from people of colour, the LGBTQ+ community, people with disabilities, neurodivergent people, parents, carers, and people from lower socio-economic backgrounds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If there's anything we can do to accommodate your specific situation, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;
